@*
    OdsContractPartyRoleSelect — a single-select pre-wired to the ContractPartyRole vocabulary
    (Odyssey Design System · components/ContractPartyRoleSelect, issue #121): what a linked record
    DOES in the agreement, each member rendered with its Material icon in its category color.

    A thin, domain-typed wrapper over the shared OdsTypeSelect — every prop passes straight through
    and this adds no behaviour, markup or state of its own, which is what lets the role field inherit
    OdsTypeSelect's accessible name, listbox semantics, keyboard model and error association rather
    than re-implementing any of them (#122 §6.1). Value is the enum key. Bind via @bind-Value.

    A plain list rather than a card grid: seven members and growing is a list, and the role is the one
    field a reader scans for. `Unspecified` is a real, selectable member — "nobody has said" — and is
    NOT the same statement as `Other`, which is the deliberate none-of-these.
*@

<OdsTypeSelect Value="@Value"
               ValueChanged="ValueChanged"
               Types="OdsTypeRegistries.ContractPartyRoles"
               Id="@Id"
               Label="@Label"
               Placeholder="@Placeholder"
               Help="@Help"
               Error="@Error"
               Required="@Required"
               Disabled="@Disabled"
               Class="@Class"
               @attributes="UserAttributes" />

@code {
    /// <summary>Selected enum key. Bindable via @bind-Value.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? Value { get; set; }

    [Parameter] public EventCallback<string> ValueChanged { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Element id for the control, so a label or a describedby can point at it.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? Id { get; set; }

    [Parameter] public string? Label { get; set; } = "Role";

    [Parameter] public string? Placeholder { get; set; } = "Select role…";

    [Parameter] public string? Help { get; set; }

    [Parameter] public string? Error { get; set; }

    [Parameter] public bool Required { get; set; }

    [Parameter] public bool Disabled { get; set; }

    [Parameter] public string? Class { get; set; }

    [Parameter(CaptureUnmatchedValues = true)]
    public Dictionary<string, object>? UserAttributes { get; set; }
}
